<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Avarayr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/451">451</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Avarayr was fought in 451 on the Avarayr plain, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a> in the historical province of Vaspurakan, between Armenian rebels led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardan-mamikonian">Vardan Mamikonian</a> and the army of the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-ii">Yazdegerd II</a>, who sought to impose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> were defeated and Vardan was killed, but resistance continued, and the Armenian Church remembers the battle as a defence of the faith.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr.jpg" alt="Battle of Avarayr" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vartanantz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
